cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  Keep the Angle: A Universal Geometry-Preserving Basis in
  Spectral Embeddings
abstract: >-
  The commute-time Laplacian embedding degenerates on large graphs (von Luxburg):
  its distances collapse to local degree. The geometry survives in the angular
  coordinate — keeping only the angle (the Ng-Jordan-Weiss row-normalization) is
  the geometrically correct projection, preserving graph geodesics universally
  across Riemannian substrates (lattices, embedding trajectories, Wolfram-model
  rewriting) while the radius is provably degenerate, and obeying a linear
  fidelity-vs-dimension law. It admits an observer-theoretic reading, developed
  and bounded with a clean negative.
